8Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"e5a58d2a5277df3837e7aac6831cc1806db9f343","github_link":"https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/commit/e5a58d2a5277df3837e7aac6831cc1806db9f343","commit_subject":"Restore the submodule commits from master","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"vpnhood/VpnHood","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:26:46Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"1f503d22ec35ab5790f6d408b035d6a114e72715","github_link":"https://github.com/vpnhood/VpnHood/commit/1f503d22ec35ab5790f6d408b035d6a114e72715","commit_subject":"Server: the shipped appsettings.json drops its ServerConfig section, so a self-hosted server no longer warns at each start that its local settings overwrote the remote configuration - LogAnonymizer true is the default, and AddListenerIpsToNetwork's null has worked as \"*\" since 2024. The server changelog says so","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"vpnhood/VpnHood","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:26:46Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"3ca978b3e90ca295c4f80da87f593ea9a95b1496","github_link":"https://github.com/vpnhood/VpnHood/commit/3ca978b3e90ca295c4f80da87f593ea9a95b1496","commit_subject":"Server: a self-hosted server serves UDP by default - on TCP's addresses, since a UDP socket on any address answers from the machine's main one, and on a port picked at its first start and kept in storage/access/udp_port, so a firewall rule made for it holds across restarts; its log names the port at each start. The settings' UdpEndPoints win: a port as it is, port 0 the kept one, [] none. A UDP listener that can't bind leaves the server on TCP, as a new test shows. The server changelog and topology's firewall line say so","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"vpnhood/VpnHood","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:26:45Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"cd10a46094321d48e377f37b22075455724af27f","github_link":"https://github.com/vpnhood/VpnHood/commit/cd10a46094321d48e377f37b22075455724af27f","commit_subject":"UDP: a client below protocol 11 gets none again, as before protocol 14 - the legacy UDP (c5b9f68ef) had dropped that limit, so v9.0.858-prerelease offered UDP to clients at protocols 8 to 10, whose datagrams it can't read. UdpDatagram.MinLegacyProtocolVersion gates the hello's port and the session's channel, and goes with the legacy UDP","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"Start9Labs/start-technologies","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:26:20Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"9e8ff880a17762060e04818f23b29267c472b850","github_link":"https://github.com/Start9Labs/start-technologies/commit/9e8ff880a17762060e04818f23b29267c472b850","commit_subject":"fix(start-os): kill image init when its launch wrapper dies (#4331)","ai_tool":"pi"},{"repo_name":"live-codes/livecodes","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:26:10Z","branch":"develop","commit_sha":"f5c6bf49bf14d786c223d6ce4003f9973e9d6f87","github_link":"https://github.com/live-codes/livecodes/commit/f5c6bf49bf14d786c223d6ce4003f9973e9d6f87","commit_subject":"i18n: add Scala (Wasm) language-info translations to all locales","ai_tool":"Pullfrog"},{"repo_name":"bex-co/beancount-io","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:25:51Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"1fe1d03e63d4b3aaa0e599c47e09959a58f19323","github_link":"https://github.com/bex-co/beancount-io/commit/1fe1d03e63d4b3aaa0e599c47e09959a58f19323","commit_subject":"chore(pm): file w21/350-353 (mobile offline cache, unconfirmed writes, logout, load more)","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"ClickHouse/ClickHouse","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:25:33Z","branch":"master","commit_sha":"664a047da07a66fa4f90f3ca3a93e94dc4f6046b","github_link":"https://github.com/ClickHouse/ClickHouse/commit/664a047da07a66fa4f90f3ca3a93e94dc4f6046b","commit_subject":"Use `index_analysis_was_already_done_on_initiator` instead of `index_analysis_skipped`","ai_tool":"Claude"},{"repo_name":"ConduitIO/conduit","commit_timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:25:23Z","branch":"main","commit_sha":"96573054fcbb3bf4d1f308129e1fdd2a95c2606d","github_link":"https://github.com/ConduitIO/c